  "answer": "### Short Answer\nTo claim a bad debt as a deductible expense, a corporation must demonstrate that the debt is considered worthless and that it has been previously included in gross income.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practice, this means that corporations should maintain thorough documentation of their accounts receivable and collection efforts. They should also ensure that any bad debts they wish to deduct have been reported as income in prior tax periods. This documentation will be crucial in case of an audit by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) to substantiate the deduction claimed.",
